<title>GERMANY: West German Oct adjusted unemployment higher.</title>
<headline>West German Oct adjusted unemployment higher.</headline>
<dateline>NUREMBERG, Germany 1996-11-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Labour Office reported the following economic indicator:</p>
<p> W.GERMAN UNEMPLOYMENT   Oct 96	 Sept 96	   Oct 95</p>
<p> Number (unadj)	    2.769 million     2.748 million	2.492 million</p>
<p> Number (adj)		2.886 million     2.856 million	2.595 million</p>
<p> Change (adj)	     +30,000	 +37,000	   n/a</p>
<p> Rate (unadj)		9.0 pct	 8.9 pct	  7.9 pct</p>
<p> Short-time workers	182,573	 152,613	  121,568</p>
<p> Vacancies		   235,105	 259,211	  231,186</p>
<p> Change in number in wrk Aug 96	  Jul 96</p>
<p>				 -58,000	 -5,000 (UNCH)</p>
<p>NOTE - Previously announced data in brackets. Numbers in work data refer to change from previous month. Details on numbers in work to be released later today.</p>
<p>---Bonn Newsroom 49-228-2609750</p>
